1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,701
Astronauts come home taller.

2
00:00:02,217 --> 00:00:04,472
In orbit, nothing squashes your spine.

3
00:00:04,472 --> 00:00:07,975
The soft discs between your vertebrae relax and spread out.

4
00:00:08,483 --> 00:00:12,087
NASA scientists say you can grow up to three percent.

5
00:00:12,087 --> 00:00:16,098
For someone 1.8 meters tall, that's about five centimeters.

6
00:00:16,583 --> 00:00:18,904
Like and subscribe for more body what-ifs.

7
00:00:19,204 --> 00:00:20,328
But there's a price.

8
00:00:20,328 --> 00:00:23,250
In one study, more than half the crew had back pain,

9
00:00:23,250 --> 00:00:26,227
and their lower back muscles shrank by about a fifth.

10
00:00:26,717 --> 00:00:30,394
Back on Earth, gravity squeezes you down again within a few months.

11
00:00:30,394 --> 00:00:33,633
And the risk of a slipped disc was about four times higher.

12
00:00:34,117 --> 00:00:36,407
So what would ten years in space do to you?

13
00:00:36,407 --> 00:00:37,792
Full story on the channel.
